From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:30:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): put comments on stored open items in their threads

Answering several items at once sends one "Comments on N items" message,
which tells the agent but leaves every stored item open in the panel until
the agent gets round to it, and the item card pieced its thread together
from the chat: the comment, then whatever sentence of the agent's next
message named the label as "Agent replied", then the closing sentence,
often the same text twice with a struck label in it.

Just before that message is sent, the browser records each stored item's
comments in the item's thread through POST /v1/sessions/{id}/open-items/
replies, named after the message (a hash of its text) so sending it again
records nothing new. The message is still one message and one turn, and the
agent finds the comments in sys_open_items_list when it starts. The send
waits at most three seconds for the record; on a server without open items
nothing is recorded, and a refused or failed call never changes the
message. An expanded row in the panel also offers Comment.

A stored item's chip previews its thread from the store (StoredItemThread:
comments and agent replies, each once, then how it was closed, without a
resolution that only repeats the last reply) instead of the comments and
sentences found in the chat. A chip of a label written only in the chat says
so and offers Record to a person who can comment, which stores it under its
own label as the panel's import does; nothing is recorded on its own.

"Comment and close", chosen per item in comment mode (the comment's header
card, the tray's toggle, or an expanded panel row), settles an item with
the comment itself. The item's heading in the message ends "(closed by me)",
so the agent knows, and before the message goes the item is closed through
PATCH /v1/sessions/{id}/open-items as the user, the comment its resolution.
It is offered only on stored items that are not closed; a close that fails
leaves the item open with its comment and says so in a toast.

Not proposed upstream yet: the comments and the store it joins are not
upstream either.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
